.TH GPS 1 2000-1月 "perturbation_channel" "perturbation_channel"
.SH NAME
perturbation_channel \- Get or set whether the perturbation channel is enabled.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIperturbation_channel(\fBgps\fR as <generic> GPSModel, 
\fBenabled\fR as integer = -1, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Get or set whether the perturbation channel is enabled.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBgps\fB \fR\- the trained model object.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenabled\fB \fR\- 
 \fB1\fR enables, \fB0\fR disables; a negative value (the default) only reads the current state.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
the currently effective flag. When enabled, the change of the perturbed gene is injected
 into the input window of its downstream targets along the prior regulatory edges, so a
 single gene knockdown does not have to survive several rounds of degree normalisation.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
GPS
.SH FILES
.PP
biosystem.dll
.PP
